  <h2 class="section-title"><span class="num">04 — Nmap</span>Nmap — The Network Mapper</h2>

  <div class="card nmap-card">
    <h4>🗺️ What is Nmap?</h4>
    <p><strong>Nmap (Network Mapper)</strong> is a free, open-source network discovery and security auditing tool created by Gordon Lyon (alias "Fyodor") in 1997. It uses raw IP packets in novel ways to determine what hosts are available on the network, what services those hosts are offering, what operating systems they are running, what type of packet filters/firewalls are in use, and dozens of other characteristics.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="analogy-box">
    <p>Imagine Nmap as a master locksmith who walks up to every door in a building and knocks in different patterns. From how doors respond — or don't respond — they can tell: Is anyone home? What kind of lock is on the door? Is there a security system? What floor are they on? All without ever entering.</p>
  </div>

