  <h3>Key Features of Nmap</h3>
  <ul class="styled">
    <li><strong>Host Discovery:</strong> Determine which IP addresses in a range have active hosts using ICMP, TCP, UDP, or ARP probes.</li>
    <li><strong>Port Scanning:</strong> Identify open, closed, and filtered ports across TCP (65,535 ports) and UDP services.</li>
    <li><strong>Service/Version Detection:</strong> Determine the application name and version running on open ports (e.g., Apache 2.4.52, OpenSSH 8.9).</li>
    <li><strong>OS Detection:</strong> Fingerprint the operating system by analyzing TCP/IP stack behaviors (timing, window sizes, TTL values).</li>
    <li><strong>Nmap Scripting Engine (NSE):</strong> Run hundreds of pre-built Lua scripts for vulnerability detection, brute forcing, and more.</li>
    <li><strong>Output Formats:</strong> Save results as normal text, XML, grepable format, or HTML for integration with other tools.</li>
    <li><strong>Firewall Evasion:</strong> Techniques like packet fragmentation, decoy scanning, and timing control to evade detection.</li>
  </ul>

