  <h2 class="section-title"><span class="num">07 — Nessus</span>Nessus — Deep Vulnerability Scanner</h2>

  <div class="card nessus-card">
    <h4>🔬 What is Nessus?</h4>
    <p><strong>Nessus</strong> is a commercial vulnerability scanner developed and maintained by <strong>Tenable, Inc.</strong> Originally open-source (1998, Renaud Deraison), it became the industry's most widely deployed dedicated vulnerability assessment tool after going commercial in 2005. Nessus goes far beyond port scanning — it performs deep inspection of running services, configurations, patch levels, and compliance status.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="analogy-box">
    <p>If Nmap is the locksmith who checks which doors exist and what locks they use, Nessus is the full-spectrum security auditor who brings in X-ray equipment, chemical analysis kits, and a compliance checklist. It doesn't just knock — it examines every detail of every door for structural weaknesses.</p>
