  <h2 class="section-title"><span class="num">09 — Scoring</span>CVSS &amp; Vulnerability Severity Scoring</h2>

  <p>Both Nessus and Nmap (via NSE) reference the <strong>Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS)</strong> to assign severity levels to discovered vulnerabilities. Understanding CVSS helps security teams prioritize remediation efficiently.</p>

  <div class="analogy-box">
    <p>CVSS is like a standardized health inspection score for vulnerabilities. Just as a restaurant inspection score tells you how serious each food safety issue is (from minor label violations to pest infestations), CVSS tells you how severe a security vulnerability is — and how urgently it needs to be fixed.</p>
  </div>

  <h3>CVSS v3.1 Scoring Metrics</h3>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h4>⚡ Attack Vector (AV)</h4>
      <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text2);">How is the vulnerability exploited? Network (worst) &gt; Adjacent &gt; Local &gt; Physical (least severe)</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h4>🔓 Attack Complexity (AC)</h4>
      <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text2);">How difficult is exploitation? Low = anyone can exploit it. High = requires specific conditions.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h4>👤 Privileges Required (PR)</h4>
      <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text2);">Does the attacker need prior access? None &gt; Low &gt; High privileges required.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h4>🤝 User Interaction (UI)</h4>
      <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text2);">Does a user need to take an action? None = more severe than Required.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>CVSS Severity Scale</h3>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="severity-bar">
      <div class="label"><span>Critical (9.0–10.0)</span><span style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;color:var(--red)">9.0 – 10.0</span></div>
      <div class="bar"><div class="fill critical" style="width:100%"></div></div>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:12px;color:var(--text3);margin:4px 0 16px;">Example: EternalBlue (CVSS 9.3), Log4Shell (CVSS 10.0). Exploit available, wide impact, no interaction needed. Patch IMMEDIATELY.</p>

    <div class="severity-bar">
      <div class="label"><span>High (7.0–8.9)</span><span style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;color:var(--orange)">7.0 – 8.9</span></div>
      <div class="bar"><div class="fill high" style="width:85%"></div></div>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:12px;color:var(--text3);margin:4px 0 16px;">Example: Heartbleed (CVSS 7.5). Significant potential for data loss. Patch within 7–30 days.</p>

    <div class="severity-bar">
      <div class="label"><span>Medium (4.0–6.9)</span><span style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;color:var(--orange)">4.0 – 6.9</span></div>
      <div class="bar"><div class="fill medium" style="width:65%"></div></div>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:12px;color:var(--text3);margin:4px 0 16px;">Requires user interaction or specific conditions. Schedule for patching in next quarterly cycle.</p>

    <div class="severity-bar">
      <div class="label"><span>Low (0.1–3.9)</span><span style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;color:var(--accent)">0.1 – 3.9</span></div>
      <div class="bar"><div class="fill low" style="width:35%"></div></div>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:12px;color:var(--text3);margin:4px 0 16px;">Minimal impact. Information disclosure, difficult to exploit. Monitor and patch in routine cycles.</p>

    <div class="severity-bar">
      <div class="label"><span>Informational (0.0)</span><span style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;color:var(--green)">0.0</span></div>
      <div class="bar"><div class="fill info" style="width:10%"></div></div>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:12px;color:var(--text3);margin:4px 0 0;">No direct vulnerability. Findings like open ports, banner information. Useful for attack surface mapping.</p>
  </div>

  <h3>CVSS Vector String Example</h3>
  <div class="code-block">
    <div class="code-label">CVE-2021-44228 — Log4Shell (CVSS 10.0)</div>
    <pre><span class="output">CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H</span>

AV:N   → Attack Vector: Network (exploitable remotely)
AC:L   → Attack Complexity: Low (easy to exploit)
PR:N   → Privileges Required: None (no auth needed)
UI:N   → User Interaction: None (fully automated)
S:C    → Scope: Changed (impacts other components)
C:H    → Confidentiality Impact: High
I:H    → Integrity Impact: High
A:H    → Availability Impact: High

<span class="comment">→ Result: CVSS Score 10.0 / Critical</span></pre>
  </div>


